    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling performance today, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (76.54) and **Christian Yelich** (75.84), our two premier starters. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a favorable matchup against Rocker, where his elite xwOBA of .469 and high-leverage order spot in the two-hole create a massive scoring foundation. Simultaneously, **Christian Yelich** capitalizes on a soft matchup against Chandler (5.12 xERA); his 100% stolen base efficiency against a slow delivery, combined with a strong platoon edge, makes him a primary target for points in our scarcest category. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.81) rounds out our top tier despite a 39% rain risk, as his leadoff status and SP skill advantage against Lodolo maintain his high floor.\n\nWhile the core of our lineup is strong, we must navigate specific risks, most notably the weather-threatened contests involving **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Lars Nootbaar** (55.37). Our most difficult roster choice was bypassing **Luke Raley** (44.34), who remained the primary candidate for a utility spot but ultimately fell short due to his lower projected efficiency and a park factor drag. We have also opted to bench **Carson Benge** (34.87) entirely, as his matchup against the elite 1.50 xERA of Rivera renders him a \"below floor\" option today. We are monitoring the lineups for **Dillon Dingler**, **Casey Schmitt**, and **Junior Caminero** closely; while **Junior Caminero** carries a solid 52.12 score, he faces a tough assignment against Gilbert, requiring a disciplined approach to preserve our game caps if the Zebras fall behind early.",
